WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.687
There is a saying: "Small capital, big

00:00:01.687 --> 00:00:03.153
power is not powerful; big capital,

00:00:03.153 --> 00:00:04.773
small power is still significant." It

00:00:04.773 --> 00:00:06.353
means that if an industry's market

00:00:06.353 --> 00:00:07.887
value is already huge, a few more

00:00:07.887 --> 00:00:09.557
percentage points of margin for TSMC

00:00:09.557 --> 00:00:11.046
would be an incredible boost for

00:00:11.046 --> 00:00:12.852
Taiwan’s entire economy, allowing for

00:00:12.852 --> 00:00:14.773
more social welfare spending. However,

00:00:14.773 --> 00:00:16.880
if an industry has a limited market,

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:18.873
even if you double its growth, its

00:00:18.873 --> 00:00:20.924
contribution to Taiwan’s economic

00:00:20.924 --> 00:00:23.202
growth and tax revenue remains limited,

00:00:23.202 --> 00:00:25.423
making it hard to fund welfare policies

00:00:25.423 --> 00:00:28.115
. So, suppose there are two industries:

00:00:28.115 --> 00:00:30.651
one can create massive export profits

00:00:30.651 --> 00:00:32.986
and keep economic growth in double

00:00:32.986 --> 00:00:35.589
digits, while the other generates less

00:00:35.589 --> 00:00:37.457
profit but creates many job

00:00:37.457 --> 00:00:39.916
opportunities. With the same resources

00:00:39.916 --> 00:00:42.113
and effort, which industry would you

00:00:42.113 --> 00:00:42.688
support?

00:00:42.688 --> 00:00:45.026
>> Because the government's role is to

00:00:45.026 --> 00:00:47.041
build an environment where all

00:00:47.041 --> 00:00:49.350
businesses can survive and thrive.

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:51.575
>> Therefore, we must help tech giants

00:00:51.575 --> 00:00:53.985
like TSMC, but we must also help small

00:00:53.985 --> 00:00:56.235
and medium-sized enterprises. As I

00:00:56.235 --> 00:00:59.097
mentioned, there are 1.71 million small

00:00:59.097 --> 00:01:01.244
and medium-sized enterprises,

00:01:01.244 --> 00:01:03.646
supporting about 9 million jobs.

00:01:03.646 --> 00:01:06.392
>> While TSMC has a massive production

00:01:06.392 --> 00:01:09.443
value in Taiwan, it only provides about

00:01:09.443 --> 00:01:12.341
90,000 jobs, so we must balance both;

00:01:12.341 --> 00:01:13.357
furthermore,

00:01:13.357 --> 00:01:15.286
>> Taiwanese society has people with

00:01:15.286 --> 00:01:17.386
diverse professional skills, and not

00:01:17.386 --> 00:01:19.076
everyone is suited for TSMC.

00:01:19.076 --> 00:01:21.442
>> TSMC also doesn't have that kind of

00:01:21.442 --> 00:01:22.134
capacity.

00:01:22.134 --> 00:01:23.878
>> So, I can take this opportunity to

00:01:23.878 --> 00:01:25.622
clarify the industrial policy I am

00:01:25.622 --> 00:01:27.416
promoting as President leading this

00:01:27.416 --> 00:01:28.065
government.

00:01:28.065 --> 00:01:30.746
>> Hmm. First, in terms of national

00:01:30.746 --> 00:01:32.901
strategic importance, the first is the

00:01:32.901 --> 00:01:34.834
"Five Trusted Industries" you just

00:01:34.834 --> 00:01:35.487
mentioned.

00:01:35.487 --> 00:01:37.861
>> That is, semiconductors, artificial

00:01:37.861 --> 00:01:40.302
intelligence, defense, security, and

00:01:40.302 --> 00:01:42.652
next-generation communications. In

00:01:42.652 --> 00:01:45.385
addition, we are also focusing on three

00:01:45.385 --> 00:01:47.808
key cores of new-era construction.

00:01:47.808 --> 00:01:51.128
>> That is, photonics. Also quantum

00:01:51.128 --> 00:01:54.463
computing, and robotics. And there are

00:01:54.463 --> 00:01:56.994
five other industries: the first is

00:01:56.994 --> 00:01:59.314
rare minerals, and the second is

00:01:59.314 --> 00:02:02.556
medical biotech. The third is

00:02:02.556 --> 00:02:05.731
infrastructure and urban renewal. The

00:02:05.731 --> 00:02:08.272
fourth is the cultural and creative

00:02:08.272 --> 00:02:11.024
industry, and the fifth is the tourism

00:02:11.024 --> 00:02:13.282
industry, totaling 13; these 13

00:02:13.282 --> 00:02:16.105
national strategic industries are being

00:02:16.105 --> 00:02:18.182
led by Premier Cho Jung-tai.

00:02:18.182 --> 00:02:19.359
>> Hmm.

00:02:19.359 --> 00:02:21.394
>> And there is another point regarding

00:02:21.394 --> 00:02:23.540
small and medium-sized enterprises, of

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:25.355
which, as I said, there are 1.71

00:02:25.355 --> 00:02:27.416
million. I have proposed the SME

00:02:27.416 --> 00:02:29.886
upgrade and transformation development

00:02:29.886 --> 00:02:32.293
act, which includes capital injection

00:02:32.293 --> 00:02:34.748
and other support. Assisting them with

00:02:34.748 --> 00:02:37.115
talent development, financial support,

00:02:37.115 --> 00:02:39.301
tax incentives, and a single-window

00:02:39.301 --> 00:02:41.304
service to help them expand into

00:02:41.304 --> 00:02:44.746
international markets. So that they can

00:02:44.746 --> 00:02:48.746
continue
